Create an IAM identity provider.

Usage:
  confluent iam identity-provider create <name> [flags]

Examples:
Create an identity provider named "demo-identity-provider".

  $ confluent iam identity-provider create demo-identity-provider --description "new description" --jwks-uri https://company.provider.com/oauth2/v1/keys --issuer-uri https://company.provider.com

Flags:
      --issuer-uri string       REQUIRED: A publicly accessible URL uniquely identifying the OAuth identity provider authorized to issue access tokens.
      --jwks-uri string         REQUIRED: A publicly accessible JSON Web Key Set (JWKS) URI for the OAuth identity provider. JWKS provides a set of cryptographic keys used to verify the authenticity and integrity of JSON Web Tokens (JWTs) issued by the OAuth identity provider.
      --description string      A description of the identity provider.
      --identity-claim string   The JSON Web Token (JWT) claim to extract the authenticating identity to Confluent resources from Registered Claim Names.
      --context string          CLI context name.
  -o, --output string           Specify the output format as "human", "json", or "yaml". (default "human")

Global Flags:
  -h, --help            Show help for this command.
      --unsafe-trace    Equivalent to -vvvv, but also log HTTP requests and responses which might contain plaintext secrets.
  -v, --verbose count   Increase verbosity (-v for warn, -vv for info, -vvv for debug, -vvvv for trace).
